[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a nice monadic and idiomatic combinator doing</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It is tempting to do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">guard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but this is not what we want here since it would just fail in <code>MetaM</code>.</p>",
        "id": 605648359,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782120158
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think if it existed it would likely be called <code>Option.guardM</code>, which we don't seem to have.</p>",
        "id": 605649519,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1782120389
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Variant:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there a more idiomatic way to do this?</p>",
        "id": 605649635,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782120410
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe a more versatile version of the non-existing <code>Option.guardM</code> would be</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">guardM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monad</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 605651799,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782120892
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does it look more familiar?</p>",
        "id": 605651878,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782120910
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There are a couple of variants in this in haskell world, xmonad has <a href=\"https://hackage.haskell.org/package/xmonad-contrib/docs/XMonad-Hooks-ManageHelpers.html#v:-45--63--62-\"><code>(-?&gt;) :: (Functor m, Monad m) =&gt; m Bool -&gt; m a -&gt; m (Maybe a)</code></a> a couple of packages also define <a href=\"https://hackage.haskell.org/package/extra/docs/Control-Monad-Extra.html#v:ifM\"><code>ifM :: Monad m =&gt; m Bool -&gt; m a -&gt; m a -&gt; m a</code></a> and one package even defines <a href=\"https://hackage.haskell.org/package/taffybar/docs/System-Taffybar-Util.html#v:maybeTCombine\"><code>maybeTCombine :: Monad m =&gt; m (Maybe a) -&gt; m (Maybe a) -&gt; m (Maybe a)</code></a>. But there doesn't seem to be a general consensus on what is the right level of abstraction from a cursory hoogle</p>",
        "id": 605655193,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1782121568
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed I played a bit with the above definitions and variants in our actual code and I kept finding new cases where we needed a more abstract version. So it may all end up in either inconsistency (when suddenly going back to bare <code>if</code>) or obfuscation if we have a super general gadget that is hard to understand.</p>",
        "id": 605658077,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1782122111
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does switching to <code>OptionT MetaM</code> has the desired semantics? <code>guard</code> and <code>&lt;|&gt;</code> of <code>OptionT</code> seem to be what is desired.</p>",
        "id": 605660809,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Miele",
        "timestamp": 1782122622
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it might be nice to have</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">macro_inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">guard?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">guardM?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monad</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(up to ascriptions and <code>m</code> typeclass generality) so we could write e.g.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">guard?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>or in the case <code>x : m α</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">guardM?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I think maybe monadicity in the <code>Bool</code> argument is a red herring, since it always has to be evaluated (compare with e.g. <code>Option.getDM</code>, where the <code>M</code> is only for the possibly-unevaluated monadic default value <code>m α</code>, not for the input <code>Option</code>).</p>",
        "id": 605780981,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1782145183
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think you can also write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">guard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(but I like the <code>Bool.guard?</code> suggestion. It could work for any <code>Alternative</code>, not just <code>Option</code>)</p>",
        "id": 605817268,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782152340
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We are also missing the <code>$&gt;</code> combinator from haskell, which would make it even shorter: <code>return (guard (←f) $&gt; x)</code></p>",
        "id": 605818273,
        "sender_full_name": "Lua Viana Reis",
        "timestamp": 1782152553
    }
]